address 170 dot 1 dot 1 dot 1 on destination port 80. The third T C P connection, similar to the previous two, originates from the client at I P address 200 dot 1 dot 1 dot 2 using source port 49726 and connects to the server at I P address 170 dot 1 dot 1 dot 1 on destination port 80. Each connection is represented by dashed arrows pointing from the client to the server, emphasizing the use of different source ports for each session while maintaining the same destination I P address and port. This setup demonstrates how multiple T C P connections can be established simultaneously from a single device to a server, each identified uniquely by its source port number. The consistent use of destination port 80 indicates that all connections are likely intended for web traffic.)/T()/K 1/Pg 760 0 R>>
