6967 0 obj
<</A 7324 0 R/S/Figure/P 6707 0 R/ActualText(In this configuration, router R 1 is connected to a cloud representing the Metro Ethernet service. A single 10-Gigabit per second access link connects R 1 to the cloud. From the Metro Ethernet cloud, three separate dashed lines are extending to remote routers R 2, R 3, and R 4, indicating three distinct E dash Line services. Each E dash Line provides a dedicated point-to-point connection between R 1 and each remote site, ensuring isolated and direct communication paths to R 2, R 3, and R 4.)/Alt(In this configuration, router R 1 is connected to a cloud representing the Metro Ethernet service. A single 10-Gigabit per second access link connects R 1 to the cloud. From the Metro Ethernet cloud, three separate dashed lines are extending to remote routers R 2, R 3, and R 4, indicating three distinct E dash Line services. Each E dash Line provides a dedicated point-to-point connection between R 1 and each remote site, ensuring isolated and direct communication paths to R 2, R 3, and R 4.)/T()/K 1/Pg 876 0 R>>
endobj

6968 0 obj
<</A 7321 0 R/S/Figure/P 6707 0 R/ActualText(In this configuration, routers R 1, R 2, R 3, and R 4 are connected to the Metro Ethernet cloud. Dashed lines represent the connections between the routers and the cloud, indicating that all routers have access to the Metro Ethernet service. Inside the cloud, additional dashed lines connect each pair of routers, forming a fully meshed network. This indicates that any router can communicate with any other router directly through the Metro Ethernet cloud.)/Alt(In this configuration, routers R 1, R 2, R 3, and R 4 are connected to the Metro Ethernet cloud. Dashed lines represent the connections between the routers and the cloud, indicating that all routers have access to the Metro Ethernet service. Inside the cloud, additional dashed lines connect each pair of routers, forming a fully meshed network. This indicates that any router can communicate with any other router directly through the Metro Ethernet cloud.)/T()/K 0/Pg 877 0 R>>
endobj

