<</A 7119 0 R/S/Figure/P 6707 0 R/ActualText(The diagram shows a packet divided into several sections. On the left, the packet starts with the "I P" and "T C P" headers, which are foundational for network communication. Following these headers, the H T T P section is depicted, starting with the "Request Header" labeled in blue. Within the request header, three key components are labeled: "Verb," "U R I," and "Some A P I Parameters." The verb represents the H T T P method \(such as GET, POST, etc.\), the U R I \(Uniform Resource Identifier\) specifies the resource being requested, and the A P I parameters provide additional information for the request. The "Verb" is labeled with an arrow pointing downwards, indicating its position within the request header. Similarly, the "U R I" and "Some A P I Parameters" are labeled with arrows pointing downwards. Next to the request header, the "Other Headers" section includes any additional headers needed for the request. Finally, the "Data" section contains the body of the request if applicable.)/Alt(The diagram shows a packet divided into several sections. On the left, the packet starts with the "I P" and "T C P" headers, which are foundational for network communication. Following these headers, the H T T P section is depicted, starting with the "Request Header" labeled in blue. Within the request header, three key components are labeled: "Verb," "U R I," and "Some A P I Parameters." The verb represents the H T T P method \(such as GET, POST, etc.\), the U R I \(Uniform Resource Identifier\) specifies the resource being requested, and the A P I parameters provide additional information for the request. The "Verb" is labeled with an arrow pointing downwards, indicating its position within the request header. Similarly, the "U R I" and "Some A P I Parameters" are labeled with arrows pointing downwards. Next to the request header, the "Other Headers" section includes any additional headers needed for the request. Finally, the "Data" section contains the body of the request if applicable.)/T()/K 0/Pg 1017 0 R>>
endobj

